From: Ajender Reddy Mallikarjuna <ajenderr@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Mon, 19 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] libbpf: fix tracepoint perf_event_open failing with -ENODEV on offline CPUs

perf_event_open_tracepoint() hardcodes cpu=0 when opening the perf event
for a tracepoint attachment. When CPU 0 is offline the syscall returns
-ENODEV and the entire BPF program attach fails.

Pass the first online CPU instead, which creates a valid per-CPU perf
event. For BPF tracepoint programs the kernel fires the program on all
CPUs regardless of the cpu argument, so any online CPU index is correct.
pid=-1 + cpu=-1 is rejected by the perf_event_open ABI with -EINVAL, so
we must pass a valid CPU index rather than -1.

Falls back to cpu=0 if the online mask cannot be read, preserving the
original behaviour on systems where the sysfs file is unavailable.

Signed-off-by: Ajender Reddy Mallikarjuna <ajenderr@qti.qualcomm.com>
---
 src/libbpf.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/libbpf.c b/src/libbpf.c
index 42bdba4..c8a3ec1 100644
--- a/src/libbpf.c
+++ b/src/libbpf.c
@@ -13069,7 +13069,8 @@ static int perf_event_open_tracepoint(const char *tp_category,
 {
 	const size_t attr_sz = sizeof(struct perf_event_attr);
 	struct perf_event_attr attr;
-	int tp_id, pfd, err;
+	bool *online = NULL;
+	int tp_id, pfd, err, cpu, n, i;

 	tp_id = determine_tracepoint_id(tp_category, tp_name);
 	if (tp_id < 0) {
@@ -13079,12 +13080,30 @@ static int perf_event_open_tracepoint(const char *tp_category,
 		return tp_id;
 	}

+	/*
+	 * Use the first online CPU. Hardcoding cpu=0 fails with -ENODEV
+	 * when CPU 0 is offline. pid=-1 + cpu=-1 is invalid per the
+	 * perf_event_open ABI, so we must pass a valid CPU index.
+	 * Fall back to cpu=0 if the online mask cannot be read.
+	 */
+	cpu = 0;
+	if (parse_cpu_mask_file("/sys/devices/system/cpu/online",
+				&online, &n) == 0) {
+		for (i = 0; i < n; i++) {
+			if (online[i]) {
+				cpu = i;
+				break;
+			}
+		}
+		free(online);
+	}
+
 	memset(&attr, 0, attr_sz);
 	attr.type = PERF_TYPE_TRACEPOINT;
 	attr.size = attr_sz;
 	attr.config = tp_id;

-	pfd = syscall(__NR_perf_event_open, &attr, -1 /* pid */, 0 /* cpu */,
+	pfd = syscall(__NR_perf_event_open, &attr, -1 /* pid */, cpu,
 		      -1 /* group_fd */, PERF_FLAG_FD_CLOEXEC);
 	if (pfd < 0) {
 		err = -errno;
--
2.34.1
